function [b_min] = dipole_field_equator(r)
%DIPOLE_FIELD_EQUATOR  The dipole field at the magnetic equator at radius r: B_min = B0 (R_E/r)^3.
%   r: real[km] (passed in m)
%   returns b_min: real[T] (passed in kg/(s^2 A))
%   Generated by tools/pcode.py from the pseudocode (trinetra-pcode/2); do not edit.
    b_min = 0;
